[al:新概念英语第二册]
[ti:17. Always Young]
[00:00.300]Passage 17 | 文章十七
[00:02.280]Always Young | 青春常驻
[00:05.590]My aunt Jennifer is an actress. | 我的姨妈詹妮弗是一位女演员。
[00:09.675]She must be at least 35 years old. | 她至少有35岁了。
[00:13.680]In spite of this, she often appears on the stage as a young girl. | 尽管如此，她仍然经常在舞台上扮演一个年轻的姑娘。
[00:19.850]Jennifer will have to take part in a new play soon. | 詹妮弗很快就要参加一个新剧的演出了。
[00:24.975]This time, she will be a girl of 17. | 这一次，她将扮演一个17岁的少女。
[00:29.790]In the play, she must appear in a bright red dress and long black stockings. | 在剧中，她必须穿一件鲜红色的连衣裙和一双黑色的长筒袜。
[00:36.805]Last year, in another play, she had to wear short socks and a bright orange-colored dress. | 去年，在另一个剧中，她不得不穿短袜和一件鲜橙色的连衣裙。
[00:45.960]If anyone ever asks her how old she is, | 如果有人问起她的年龄，
[00:49.970]she always answers, "My dear, it must be terrible to be grown up!" | 她总是回答说：“亲爱的，长大一定很糟糕！”